# MANDATORY STOP POINTS & OUTPUT RULES

> Anti-patterns, RGV self-check, output separation enforcement, micro-checkpoint rules.
> This agent uses **continuous processing** with per-section micro-checkpoints — no user stops between phases.

---

## CORE PRINCIPLE: CONTINUOUS PROCESSING WITH MICRO-CHECKPOINTS

This agent does NOT stop for user confirmation between phases. The only stop point is **before starting** (to confirm input folder). Within phases, each section follows the RGV loop (`@01_Guidance.mdc §1`) with a mandatory micro-checkpoint.

```
At START:
1. CONFIRM input folder with user
2. READ templates and examples
3. PROCESS all 6 phases automatically with per-section RGV loops
4. PRESENT final summary with micro-checkpoint rollup
```

---

## 1 MANDATORY STOP POINT

| # | Phase | Trigger | Present | Wait For |
|---|-------|---------|---------|----------|
| 1 | Before Phase 0 | User provides input folder | Input folder contents, component count estimate | Explicit "proceed" or folder correction |

After this single confirmation, **process all 6 phases continuously** with micro-checkpoints per section and auto checkpoints per phase.

