## ❌ ANTI-PATTERNS (FORBIDDEN)

### RGV Anti-Patterns
```
❌ Generating ANY table without first counting elements in XML (skipping INVENTORY)
❌ Proceeding to next section without verifying generated count = XML count (skipping VERIFY)
❌ Skipping INVENTORY step "because the map is small"
❌ Generating mapping tables from Phase 0 memory without RE-READING the map XML
❌ Generating flow steps from Phase 0 memory without RE-READING the process XML
❌ Documenting profiles without RE-READING the profile XML
❌ Reading map XML alone without also reading source/target profile XMLs for field paths
❌ Skipping micro-checkpoint after completing a section
```

### Extraction Anti-Patterns
```
❌ Using Python/Bash scripts for XML extraction
❌ "Representative samples" or "key mappings" for large tables
❌ "Showing X of Y" with note about remaining
❌ Collapsed/merged rows for similar patterns
❌ "0 rows" for cross-reference tables
❌ Summarizing or truncating script code
❌ Only documenting mapped profile fields
❌ Generic shape descriptions instead of complete config
```

### Output Anti-Patterns
```
❌ Shape Count Verification block in main document
❌ Mapping Count Verification block in main document
❌ Abbreviated mapping tables in main document
❌ Summarized shape tables in main document
❌ Verification status badges (✅ MATCH) in main document sections 3-4
```

### Phase Boundary Anti-Patterns
```
❌ Generating profile/function supporting docs in Phase 2 (belongs in Phase 3)
❌ Generating connector/crossref supporting docs in Phase 2 (belongs in Phase 4)
❌ "Should I continue with Phase 2?"
❌ "Ready to proceed to Phase 3?"
❌ "Would you like me to continue?"
❌ "I'll proceed while waiting..."
❌ "Assuming you agree..."
❌ Making assumptions about missing XML data
❌ Inferring behavior not explicit in XML
```

